        "original_id": "d3b4dcf7-e09a-55e5-9fc4-93073318a6eb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Trax Colton, Louis A. Morelli, Andrew Marton, Jayne Mansfield, Roger Browne, Maria Xénia, Nico Minardos, Bob Mathias\n- Companies: 20th Century Fox, 21st Century Fox\n- Films: It Happened in Athens\n- Places: Century City, Los Angeles, Beverly Hills\n- Roles: motion picture actor, contract player, director\n- Topics: American film studios, Big Six\n\nFacts:\n- Trax Colton, born Louis A. Morelli on May 26, 1929, is an American former motion picture actor.\n- Between 1960 and 1962, Trax Colton appeared in two films as a contract player for 20th Century Fox.\n- It Happened in Athens was directed by Andrew Marton.\n- It Happened in Athens features Jayne Mansfield, Trax Colton, Roger Browne in his debut, Maria Xénia, Nico Minardos, and Bob Mathias.\n- Twentieth Century Fox Film Corporation used the hyphenated name Twentieth Century-Fox Film Corporation from 1935 until 1985.\n- 20th Century Fox is an American film studio currently owned by 21st Century Fox.\n- 20th Century Fox is one of the Big Six major American film studios.\n- 20th Century Fox is located in Century City in Los Angeles, just west of Beverly Hills.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5250dcf5-72d0-58d3-8566-cbbd3ffc0569",
